WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:06.160
President Joe Biden, who some on the&nbsp;
left framed as a neo liberal warmonger,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:13.840
thirsty for wars and colonialism around the&nbsp;
world, wants to completely reexamine and evaluate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:20.960
the global troop presence of the United States&nbsp;
and maybe decrease it in some significant way. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.960 --> 00:00:26.400
what's interesting about this story, it's not&nbsp;
been getting a lot of attention, and it's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.120
surprising to me that it's not getting a lot of&nbsp;
attention because this is the exact type of story&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.120 --> 00:00:36.080
that does terribly when we talk about it,&nbsp;
because the sensible left is sort of like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:42.000
yeah, we sort of knew that Biden wasn't a&nbsp;
bloodthirsty warmonger. So this isn't surprising.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:48.640
The anti Biden left just doesn't want to hear&nbsp;
it because it runs counter to their narrative&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:54.000
and it's really what the right expects. I mean,&nbsp;
I know that the right under Trump cheered this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.920
talking point of Trump didn't start any new&nbsp;
wars, but it's not actually their preferred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:08.000
position on foreign policy. The preferred position&nbsp;
of the reactionary right is Democratic presidents&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:12.880
are weak because they don't want to use the&nbsp;
military and they often want to shrink the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:18.320
military. That's the lane in which the right is&nbsp;
most comfortable critiquing Democratic presidents.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:24.560
So the news is to start at the beginning that&nbsp;
the Joe Biden administration has launched a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:30.240
full systemic review of the global presence of&nbsp;
the U.S. military to ensure that it is, quote,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.240 --> 00:01:37.520
correctly sized and supports strategy. So at the&nbsp;
top, that's not the language of our military's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.520 --> 00:01:41.280
presence is too small and we should figure&nbsp;
out ways to make it much bigger. That's kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:46.480
of the starting point. Foreign policy analysts&nbsp;
believe that this is exactly the type of review&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:52.320
that could lead to recommendations to reduce&nbsp;
the number of bases abroad, something I've been&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:57.440
talking about for a decade, reduce the number of&nbsp;
troops deployed around the world. Now, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:57.440 --> 00:02:03.360
we should all be skeptical that it will turn into&nbsp;
action, given two things. Number one, given all of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:09.520
the different ways that Republicans can obstruct,&nbsp;
we have to wonder whether even a recommendation of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:14.640
reducing the U.S. global troop presence will&nbsp;
turn into into a reality. On the other hand,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:18.640
we've also heard this from other presidents,&nbsp;
right? I mean, we we heard this from Obama.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:24.160
We've even heard it from Republican presidents and&nbsp;
rarely do things change dramatically. Right now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.160 --> 00:02:30.240
the US has about 800 quote, bases around the&nbsp;
world. It's an incredible top number. The truth&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:30.240 --> 00:02:36.720
is that includes some very small outposts that few&nbsp;
of us would see a picture of and say that's a base&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:44.480
all the way up to massive complexes with thousands&nbsp;
of troops and their families. I mean, just huge&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:49.760
installations. Germany is a place where there&nbsp;
are many there are some in Italy. Many of these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:55.680
are essentially vestiges of the Cold War that we&nbsp;
really don't need and arguably are a detriment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.680 --> 00:03:01.440
to American foreign policy. And for me, this&nbsp;
is not just a moral issue, although it is one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.480
but it's also an economic issue. We talk&nbsp;
about tax rates and how we can afford things&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:11.600
that some want to do. Putting aside for a&nbsp;
second modern monetary theory and a more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:12.320 --> 00:03:17.200
nuanced understanding of debt and deficit. And&nbsp;
putting aside the macroeconomic discussion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:24.400
the micro of the budget is not trivial. Half of&nbsp;
American discretionary spending is on military&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:28.720
and defense. So we can talk about tax rates,&nbsp;
of course. And last week we talked about, OK,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:33.280
do should we raise taxes on people making over&nbsp;
400000 or over a million or over two million?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:39.280
Where should it be? But imagine without.&nbsp;
Changing anything about taxation, taxation,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:46.880
what we could afford with current tax revenues,&nbsp;
if we change spending priorities and reduce the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.880 --> 00:03:51.600
amount that we're spending on defense and&nbsp;
the military, and without a doubt, there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:58.160
a huge I'll believe it when I see it component,&nbsp;
as I mentioned earlier. But this is sort of like a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:04.720
wow, what what is the truth of Biden's&nbsp;
foreign policy? And to be clear,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:10.400
this is not a wow. Biden is the super progressive&nbsp;
on foreign policy. Absolutely not. That's not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.400 --> 00:04:15.280
what I'm saying. The point here is just like&nbsp;
some on the left insisted Hillary would have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:19.920
started five new wars and there was really no&nbsp;
reason to believe that that's what would happen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:20.720 --> 00:04:25.280
The people expecting Biden to do the same&nbsp;
and to grow the troop presence are going to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:32.000
be disappointed. Now, Joe Biden did decide&nbsp;
to pause and reexamine troop withdrawals&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.640
that were started or at least announced by Donald&nbsp;
Trump. I'm talking about Afghanistan and Germany,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.640 --> 00:04:40.320
where Trump said, let's pull out. And Joe Biden&nbsp;
got in and said, we're going to pause that.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.120 --> 00:04:46.480
Let's wait and see, OK? Because the position&nbsp;
of the Biden administration is essentially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.480 --> 00:04:52.400
these are my words, not theirs. But this is the&nbsp;
way I understand it. Trump was so incompetent that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:58.240
it's worth reviewing everything Trump was in the&nbsp;
middle of before we decide whether to continue it.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.240 --> 00:05:03.040
My hope is that Biden reviews those two&nbsp;
withdrawals, Germany and Afghanistan,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:09.120
and does this bigger reevaluation and says,&nbsp;
let's continue and then let's do more.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:16.160
At the same time, troops in Germany is far&nbsp;
less controversial than many other deployments.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.160 --> 00:05:21.440
And so I think that the U.S. has a&nbsp;
comically high number of bases in Germany&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.440 --> 00:05:26.160
and many of them are completely unnecessary. I&nbsp;
don't know that I would have would have started in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:30.880
Germany necessarily. When I think about reducing&nbsp;
our troops spread around the world, it doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.880 --> 00:05:35.520
matter. The point is we're going to wait and&nbsp;
see what Joe Biden actually decides on those&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.520 --> 00:05:40.800
two. We're also going to see what the outcome&nbsp;
is of this systemic review of the global troop&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:44.480
presence around the world. And I'm not I know&nbsp;
some people will write to me and say, David,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:49.840
you're so naive. He's not doing anything.&nbsp;
The point is, there was a narrative about.&nbsp;&nbsp;

